## THE CORE BUG THAT WAS DIAGNOSED AND FIXED (important context)

Running raw OHRC lunar crops through Depth Anything V2 produced a **smooth sloped surface instead of real crater structure**. Root cause: the model (trained on natural photos) reads the image's broad sun-angle lighting gradient as "depth" and under-weights the actual small crater shadows. Confirmed visually against a real 2000x2000 OHRC crop (sun_elevation=-0.17deg, near-horizon grazing light).

**Fix built:** `lunar_preprocess.py` — (1) gradient-flatten via high-pass filter (heavy Gaussian blur, subtract), (2) CLAHE local contrast enhancement. Auto-detected via `looks_like_lunar_grayscale()` (checks if R/G/B channels are near-identical, meaning grayscale-saved-as-RGB). Every step emits live progress events for the terminal UI.

