## Also fixed in the same pass: realistic depth scaling

`pointcloud.py` used to hardcode `depth_scale=40.0` (arbitrary). Now has `compute_realistic_depth_scale(image_width_px, pixel_resolution_m)` which derives scale from real ground sample distance (e.g. 0.24 m/px for the OHRC dataset) assuming ~10% relief-to-width ratio for simple lunar craters (a stated, defensible geomorphology assumption, not a measurement). `server.py`'s `_run_pipeline` now accepts an optional `pixel_resolution_m` param, adjusts it correctly if the image gets resized, and passes it through. Frontend needs a small input field + payload field to actually use this (see FPV_FLYTHROUGH_PATCH.md step 2-3, already written).

